          "rules": [
            {
              "deprecatedIds": [
                "CVE-2020-14343",
                "PYSEC-2021-142",
                "GHSA-8q59-q68h-6hv4"
              ],
              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "A vulnerability was discovered in the PyYAML library in versions before 5.4, where it is susceptible to arbitrary code execution when it processes untrusted YAML files through the full_load method or with the FullLoader loader. Applications that use the library to process untrusted input may be vulnerable to this flaw. This flaw allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code on the system by abusing the python/object/new constructor. This flaw is due to an incomplete fix for CVE-2020-1747.",
                "text": "A vulnerability was discovered in the PyYAML library in versions before 5.4, where it is susceptible to arbitrary code execution when it processes untrusted YAML files through the full_load method or with the FullLoader loader. Applications that use the library to process untrusted input may be vulnerable to this flaw. This flaw allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code on the system by abusing the python/object/new constructor. This flaw is due to an incomplete fix for CVE-2020-1747."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2020-14343](https://osv.dev/CVE-2020-14343)**\n(Also published as: [PYSEC-2021-142](https://osv.dev/PYSEC-2021-142), [GHSA-8q59-q68h-6hv4](https://osv.dev/GHSA-8q59-q68h-6hv4), ).\n\n## [PYSEC-2021-142](https://osv.dev/PYSEC-2021-142)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e A vulnerability was discovered in the PyYAML library in versions before 5.4, where it is susceptible to arbitrary code execution when it processes untrusted YAML files through the full_load method or with the FullLoader loader. Applications that use the library to process untrusted input may be vulnerable to this flaw. This flaw allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code on the system by abusing the python/object/new constructor. This flaw is due to an incomplete fix for CVE-2020-1747.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n## [GHSA-8q59-q68h-6hv4](https://osv.dev/GHSA-8q59-q68h-6hv4)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e A vulnerability was discovered in the PyYAML library in versions before 5.4, where it is susceptible to arbitrary code execution when it processes untrusted YAML files through the full_load method or with the FullLoader loader. Applications that use the library to process untrusted input may be vulnerable to this flaw. This flaw allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code on the system by abusing the python/object/new constructor. This flaw is due to an incomplete fix for CVE-2020-1747.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/src/lab5-canary/requirements.txt | pyyaml | 5.3.1 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-8q59-q68h-6hv4 | pyyaml | 5.4 |\n| PYSEC-2021-142 | pyyaml | 5.4 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/src/lab5-canary/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2020-14343\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2020-14343](https://osv.dev/CVE-2020-14343)**\n(Also published as: [PYSEC-2021-142](https://osv.dev/PYSEC-2021-142), [GHSA-8q59-q68h-6hv4](https://osv.dev/GHSA-8q59-q68h-6hv4), ).\n\n## [PYSEC-2021-142](https://osv.dev/PYSEC-2021-142)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e A vulnerability was discovered in the PyYAML library in versions before 5.4, where it is susceptible to arbitrary code execution when it processes untrusted YAML files through the full_load method or with the FullLoader loader. Applications that use the library to process untrusted input may be vulnerable to this flaw. This flaw allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code on the system by abusing the python/object/new constructor. This flaw is due to an incomplete fix for CVE-2020-1747.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n## [GHSA-8q59-q68h-6hv4](https://osv.dev/GHSA-8q59-q68h-6hv4)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e A vulnerability was discovered in the PyYAML library in versions before 5.4, where it is susceptible to arbitrary code execution when it processes untrusted YAML files through the full_load method or with the FullLoader loader. Applications that use the library to process untrusted input may be vulnerable to this flaw. This flaw allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code on the system by abusing the python/object/new constructor. This flaw is due to an incomplete fix for CVE-2020-1747.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/src/lab5-canary/requirements.txt | pyyaml | 5.3.1 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-8q59-q68h-6hv4 | pyyaml | 5.4 |\n| PYSEC-2021-142 | pyyaml | 5.4 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/src/lab5-canary/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2020-14343\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
              },
              "id": "CVE-2020-14343",
              "name": "CVE-2020-14343",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              },
              "relationships": [],
              "shortDescription": {
                "markdown": "CVE-2020-14343: Improper Input Validation in PyYAML",
                "text": "CVE-2020-14343: Improper Input Validation in PyYAML"
              }
            },
            {
              "deprecatedIds": [
                "CVE-2024-47081",
                "PYSEC-2026-1872",
                "GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7"
              ],
              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "### Impact\n\nDue to a URL parsing issue, Requests releases prior to 2.32.4 may leak .netrc credentials to third parties for specific maliciously-crafted URLs.\n\n### Workarounds\nFor older versions of Requests, use of the .netrc file can be disabled with `trust_env=False` on your Requests Session ([docs](https://requests.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/#requests.Session.trust_env)).\n\n### References\nhttps://github.com/psf/requests/pull/6965\nhttps://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/Jun/2",
                "text": "### Impact\n\nDue to a URL parsing issue, Requests releases prior to 2.32.4 may leak .netrc credentials to third parties for specific maliciously-crafted URLs.\n\n### Workarounds\nFor older versions of Requests, use of the .netrc file can be disabled with `trust_env=False` on your Requests Session ([docs](https://requests.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/#requests.Session.trust_env)).\n\n### References\nhttps://github.com/psf/requests/pull/6965\nhttps://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/Jun/2"
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2024-47081](https://osv.dev/CVE-2024-47081)**\n(Also published as: [PYSEC-2026-1872](https://osv.dev/PYSEC-2026-1872), [GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7](https://osv.dev/GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7), ).\n\n## [PYSEC-2026-1872](https://osv.dev/PYSEC-2026-1872)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Due to a URL parsing issue, Requests releases prior to 2.32.4 may leak .netrc credentials to third parties for specific maliciously-crafted URLs.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e For older versions of Requests, use of the .netrc file can be disabled with `trust_env=False` on your Requests Session ([docs](https://requests.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/#requests.Session.trust_env)).\n\u003e \n\u003e ### References\n\u003e https://github.com/psf/requests/pull/6965\n\u003e https://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/Jun/2\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n## [GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7](https://osv.dev/GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Due to a URL parsing issue, Requests releases prior to 2.32.4 may leak .netrc credentials to third parties for specific maliciously-crafted URLs.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e For older versions of Requests, use of the .netrc file can be disabled with `trust_env=False` on your Requests Session ([docs](https://requests.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/#requests.Session.trust_env)).\n\u003e \n\u003e ### References\n\u003e https://github.com/psf/requests/pull/6965\n\u003e https://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/Jun/2\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/src/lab5-canary/requirements.txt | requests | 2.19.1 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7 | requests | 2.32.4 |\n| PYSEC-2026-1872 | requests | 2.32.4 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/src/lab5-canary/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2024-47081\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2024-47081](https://osv.dev/CVE-2024-47081)**\n(Also published as: [PYSEC-2026-1872](https://osv.dev/PYSEC-2026-1872), [GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7](https://osv.dev/GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7), ).\n\n## [PYSEC-2026-1872](https://osv.dev/PYSEC-2026-1872)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Due to a URL parsing issue, Requests releases prior to 2.32.4 may leak .netrc credentials to third parties for specific maliciously-crafted URLs.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e For older versions of Requests, use of the .netrc file can be disabled with `trust_env=False` on your Requests Session ([docs](https://requests.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/#requests.Session.trust_env)).\n\u003e \n\u003e ### References\n\u003e https://github.com/psf/requests/pull/6965\n\u003e https://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/Jun/2\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n## [GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7](https://osv.dev/GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Due to a URL parsing issue, Requests releases prior to 2.32.4 may leak .netrc credentials to third parties for specific maliciously-crafted URLs.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e For older versions of Requests, use of the .netrc file can be disabled with `trust_env=False` on your Requests Session ([docs](https://requests.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/#requests.Session.trust_env)).\n\u003e \n\u003e ### References\n\u003e https://github.com/psf/requests/pull/6965\n\u003e https://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/Jun/2\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/src/lab5-canary/requirements.txt | requests | 2.19.1 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7 | requests | 2.32.4 |\n| PYSEC-2026-1872 | requests | 2.32.4 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/src/lab5-canary/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2024-47081\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
